## Hints for Future Agents
If K3-on-CUDA-12 is ever needed: attn_res.py:191 gates the native kernel on
current_platform.is_device_capability_family(100) only, while kda.py:74 also
checks hasattr(torch.ops._C, "fused_kda_decode"). Adding the same hasattr
guard to attn_res would make K3 fall back to its (existing, unreachable)
Triton path under CUDA 12 -- upstream-worthy, perf unmeasured. The dead cu12
images remain in the dev registry as vllm-k3{,-infr}:arm64-658f2f56-cu1291-r1.

## Codebase Discoveries
The cu12.9 vllm entry predates K3 by two releases (present at v0.25.1) and no
file in the repo documents why it exists -- treat it as load-bearing for an
unknown consumer until someone identifies them.

